  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">⁊ sawlsceat is rihtast þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man gelæste æt ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> openu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="20" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ saulsceat is rihtast þæt man symble gelæste aa æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And saulsceat is rihtast, þæt man symble gelæste aa æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And it is best that payment for the souls of the dead should always be rendered before the grave is closed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And it is most appropriate that dues for the souls of the dead always be paid while the grave is yet open.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Seelengeld ist am richtigsten, dass man immer sofort entrichte beim offenen Grabe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And as for soul-scot, it is most right that it always be paid at once at the open grave.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
